   "shape_m": "p",
   "html_text": "Representationalists hold that, quite generally, the properties of a representational vehicle (that which is doing the representing) and the content of that representation (what is represented) need to be sharply distinguished. The word “red” can represent the colour red without itself being red. A copy of a newspaper is very different from the stories it tells. In the case of temporal experience anyone who finds this theory of perception appealing can adopt a quite straightforward position on t",
